Paint by Julian Toler
=====================
Freeware! feel free to hack the source code and if you make
improvements (I mean keep it small but make it better!) send
a copy back to Steve Lichfield at 3Lib.

The program is a type 0 OPA (i.e. it does not understand file
commands sent to it from the system screen).  I consider that
this is in keeping with the way the program is designed to
work and besides it helps to keep down the file size!

The help file (PAINTHLP.OPO) should be in either the standard
\OPO directory or for tidiness can be tucked away in an
\APP\PAINT directory.  This file can be deleted without
problems if required to save space. 

Quick Overview
==============
The program treats the screen as workspace, upon which
pictures can be loaded, cut and generally fiddled around
with.  A useful feature is the ability to grab icon sized
chunks of screen (48x48 bitmaps in black and grey) as well as
the facility to resize the workspace at will (up to the limit
of memory).  Some funny things start happening at extremes of
memory limitation so save before over extending!

HELP
====
Here is the help file with programming code chopped out:

Help: Paint
þGeneral principles
þMenu options

Help: General Principles
Paint is a simple but capable drawing package.
The program has been designed to be compact with only a few bells
and whistles. For example, the cut/paste feature of many Psion
applications has not been implimented, however it is possible to
cut and save an area of the screen and this may be re-loaded as a
file if required. The program is perfect for routine tasks such as
icon design. I hope it is found useful.


