Help: File Menu
þOpen
þSave
þSave Area
þSave icon
þExit
þAbout

Help: File Open
Opens a PIC file and paste anywhere on the screen.
The picture may be loaded one colour plane at a time
or both together.  Grey may be copied to black and
vice versa (if vice is your cup of tea).
If you try to load a grey plane when no such plane
is present in the file, an error is reported.

Help: File Save Entire Picture
Options to save black, grey or both colours
to a file.  Please note that there is no error
checking on the existance of specified
directories or memory availability (SORRY!).

Help: File Save Area
Provides a rubber band box to select area to save to file.
A small cursor will be seen. This may be obscured
by your drawing so move it around a bit until it is visible.
Press enter to set the top left corner of the save box,
then drag out a box enclosing the area to be saved.
Press enter again to complete the area selection.

Help: File Save Icon
Provides a moveable 48 ž 48 pixel box to
select area to save as a Series 3a icon file.
Both black and grey planes are captured.

Help: File Exit
Quits the application.
Beware, no files are saved!

Help: About
A brief advert for yours truly.

Help: Draw
þBrush
þRectangle
þElipse/Circle
þLine
þText

Help: Brush
In brush mode, holding SHIFT and moving the cursor will apply
the selected colour(s), whereas holding down CONTROL will
delete pixels in the selected colour(s). Use the menu or
hot keys to switch colours. Use +/- to increase/decrease the
size of the brush. Use PSION key to speed up cursor movement.
Simulate an eraser by selecting Combined and hold CONTROL
while moving the cursor. Use PSION-F to find a lost cursor!

Help: Rectangle
Provides a rubber band box to select rectangle area.
A (very) small cursor will be seen. This may be obscured
by your drawing so move it around a bit until it is visible.
Press enter to set the top left corner of the rectangle,
then drag out the rectangle to the desired size.
Press enter again to complete the area selection.
Select coordinate display for accurate position/size.

Help: Circle/Elipse
Use the dialog to select options required. Note that the
Relative Height option provides the opportunity to draw
elipses as well as regular circles.
Choose the centre of the circle/elipse by moving the cursor
and pressing ENTER.

Help: Text
After choosing options and entering text,
the program allows precise placement on the screen.
Use suitable colours/modes with slight displacement
to create shadow effects.

Help: Line
Single or continuous lines may be drawn.
Fix a point on a continuous line using
the space bar.  Start and Terminate
lines by pressing Enter.

Help: Options
þBorder
þClear screen
þShow/hide coordinates
þMove
þResize
þPicture information

Help: Border
Draws a one pixel border around (inside of) the picture.
This makes it easier to see the edges, but note that this
border is part of the picture and is saved when using the
Psion-S option.  De-selecting the border removes a one
pixel strip around the edge of the picture.

Help: Clear Screen
Clears the screen and resets
window to 416 ž 160 pixels.
NO PICTURE IS SAVED!,$300

Help: Show/Hide Coordinates
Coordinate display (x ž y) is available
when using the brush, drawing rectangles,
or placing text etc. and can be enabled or
disabled using this option.

Help: Move
This feature is essential for pictures having
dimensions greater than the screen (480 ž 160)
The picture can be shifted to allow viewing
or editing. Save large pictures using the Save
(Psion-S) option rather than Save Area.

Help: Information
Provides the following statistics:
Screen width and height
Point of origin for the current picture window
Free memory (approximate but close enough!)
